<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of the Himyarites</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of the Himyarites is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac">Syriac</a> Christian work of the 6th century that recounts the persecution of the Christians of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najran">Najran</a> under the Himyarite king Yusuf, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-nuwas">Dhu Nuwas</a>, and the Aksumite invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> that followed. It survives only in fragments of a single <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>, published by Axel Moberg in 1924, and is a key source for the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himyarite-kingdom">Himyarite Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
